{#
  CSI Lab · UFOP — shared macros (foundation).

  Import them WITH CONTEXT — btn/link_arrow read data.ui.common.new_tab and avatar reads base_path:
    {% from "_macros.njk" import icon, brand, section_head, page_header, page_toc, btn, link_arrow, chip, status_chip, avatar, person_id, stat with context %}

  icon(name, size=20, class="")      24×24 stroke icon, stroke 1.75, currentColor, aria-hidden.
                                     Geometry adapted from Lucide (ISC License, © Lucide Contributors).
  brand(name, size=20, class="")     filled glyphs: twitter, instagram, github, scholar, lattes, orcid.
                                     Paths adapted from Simple Icons (CC0); lattes is a monogram.
  section_head(index, eyebrow, title, sub=none, id=none, align="start", level=2, layout="stack", meta=none, reveal=true)
                                     index: "01" or 1 (zero-padded); id goes on the heading;
                                     align: "start" | "center"; sub: text or `| mdi` output.
                                     layout "split": eyebrow + title left (7fr), meta + lead right
                                     (5fr) from 960px; meta: a short mono note ("7 pessoas").
                                     The head reveals itself (data-reveal): don't wrap it in another
                                     [data-reveal]; reveal=false for a head in the first screen.
  page_header(label, title, sub=none, aside=false)
                                     inner-page hero with grid + glow; renders the page's only <h1>.
                                     {% call page_header(...) %}…{% endcall %} adds content below the sub.
                                     aside=true: a second column from 1100px, filled by the same call
                                     block, which then receives the slot name:
                                     {% call(slot) page_header(l, t, s, aside=true) %}{% if slot == "aside" %}…{% else %}…{% endif %}{% endcall %}
  page_toc(items, label, sticky=false)
                                     in-page nav strip, called right after page_header at the top level
                                     of the content block (a direct child of <main>). items: [{ href,
                                     label, count? }]. sticky: pinned under the header, scroll-spy
                                     (site.js); the root scroll padding then clears it.
  btn(href, label, variant="primary", icon=none, external=false, aria_label=none)
                                     variant: "primary" | "ghost"; icon: any icon() name; aria_label
                                     replaces the accessible name (it must contain the visible label).
  link_arrow(href, label, external=false, icon=none, class="")
                                     text link with a sliding arrow; the last word and the arrow never
                                     break apart; icon: e.g. "arrow-up" for a link back up the page;
                                     class: extra classes on the <a>, e.g. "card__link".
  chip(label, href=none, current=false, class="", count=none)
                                     current → aria-current="true" (red tint + leading dot);
                                     class: e.g. "chip--nowrap" inside a horizontal scroller;
                                     count → <span class="chip__count">.
  status_chip(status, label)         project status: "active" | "development" | "completed".
  avatar(person, size="md", alt="")  photo (person.photo) or ridge monogram (person.name | monogram);
                                     size sm 40 | md 64 | lg 96 | xl 144. Decorative by default (the
                                     name is adjacent text); put data-person on the element that stands
                                     for the person (hover/focus ring, photo colour).
  person_id(person, level="h3")      name (h3/h4/p/strong) with the role in grey mono capitals above it.
  stat(value, suffix="", label="", size="md")
                                     big number + mono label; counts up when visible (site.js);
                                     size: "sm" | "md" | "xl" (one feature stat per page).
#}

